+## Normal death EXP loss — candidate October 17
+
+The owner requested no normal-death EXP penalty. The reviewed candidate sets
+existing default rule `Character:DeathExpLossLevel=256`; all uint8 player levels
+then receive zero `exploss` before `SetEXP` and corpse creation. Multiplier index
+zero still loses 0.5%, so it is not a disable switch. Old corpse recovery remains;
+new zero-loss corpses cannot grant resurrection EXP. AA, other death mechanics,
+and Sacrifice's separate reagent cost stay unchanged. No retroactive XP refund.
+
+Source and tests: `server-mods/code/zone/attack.cpp` (`Client::Death`),
+`client_process.cpp` (`OPRezzAnswer`), `exp.cpp` (level warning), `ruletypes.h`,
+and `tools/tests/test_no_death_exp_loss.py` in
+`E:/EQ_Local_Dev/_worktrees/no-death-exp-loss` (8d30ea6 + reviewed candidate).
+The compiled decision/application passes 2,048 cases and two old-policy controls;
+resurrection/corpse source checks pass. This is not a full server build or live QA.
+
+`docs/ops/no-death-exp-loss-20261017/` owns guarded forward/inverse SQL, preflight,
+recovery and exact owner QA. Read-only OVH verification at 13:47 UTC October17
+still observes default value10, with no ruleset overrides and current dungeon
+world/zone hashes. Other rulesets inherit default before their own values.
+Activation needs fresh backup/preimages and verified world/all-zone Rules reload;
+no restart, client, quest or cache pairing. Never deploy this older full overlay
+over retained production binaries. Main/OVH approval, activation, owner gameplay
+QA and prepared wiki publication remain pending; this is not a live-state change.
+
